<dl>
<dt>Source:
<dd><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Script.ldf" title="Script.ldf">script.ldf</a>
<dt>Sent when:
<dd>A plot is setting a plot flag
<dt>Sent from:
<dd><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Engine" title="Engine (page does not exist)">engine</a>
<dt>Sent to:
<dd>plot script
<dt>Parameters:
<dd>
<ul>
<li>Creator: owner of the plot table, should be a player</li><li>Integer 1: bit flag number being affected</li><li>Integer 2: the value about to be written (on a normal SET that should be '1', and on a 'clear' it should be '0')</li><li>Integer 3: On SET call, the current flag value (can be either 1 or 0 regardless if it's a set or clear event)</li><li>Integer 4: 1 if the current flag (Int 1) is defined, 0 for normal flag.</li><li>String 0: plot GUID, defined as string constant</li>
</ul>
</dl>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Usage">Usage</span></h3>
<div class="dascript" style="font-family:monospace; background-color:#F9F9F9; border: 1px dashed #2F6FAB; white-space:pre; line-height:1.25em; padding:1.0em;"><span style="color: #0000FF;"><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Case%20keyword" title="Case keyword (page does not exist)">case</a></span> EVENT_TYPE_SET_PLOT:<br />{<br />    <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Object%20keyword" title="Object keyword">object</a> oCreator = <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/GetEventCreator" title="GetEventCreator">GetEventCreator</a>(ev); <span style="color: #007F00; font-style: italic;">// owner of the plot table, should be a player</span><br />    <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Int%20keyword" title="Int keyword">int</a> nFlag = <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/GetEventInteger" title="GetEventInteger">GetEventInteger</a>(ev, <span style="color: #7F007F;">1</span>); <span style="color: #007F00; font-style: italic;">// bit flag number being affected</span><br />    <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Int%20keyword" title="Int keyword">int</a> nValue = <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/GetEventInteger" title="GetEventInteger">GetEventInteger</a>(ev, <span style="color: #7F007F;">2</span>); <span style="color: #007F00; font-style: italic;">// the value about to be written (on a normal SET that should be '1', and on a 'clear' it should be '0')</span><br />    <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Int%20keyword" title="Int keyword">int</a> nOldValue = <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/GetEventInteger" title="GetEventInteger">GetEventInteger</a>(ev, <span style="color: #7F007F;">3</span>); <span style="color: #007F00; font-style: italic;">// On SET call, the current flag value (can be either 1 or 0 regardless if it's a set or clear event)</span><br />    <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Int%20keyword" title="Int keyword">int</a> nIsDefined = <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/GetEventInteger" title="GetEventInteger">GetEventInteger</a>(ev, <span style="color: #7F007F;">4</span>); <span style="color: #007F00; font-style: italic;">// 1 if the current flag (Int 1) is defined, 0 for normal flag.</span><br />    <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/String%20keyword" title="String keyword">string</a> sPlot = <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/GetEventString" title="GetEventString">GetEventString</a>(ev, <span style="color: #7F007F;">0</span>); <span style="color: #007F00; font-style: italic;">// plot GUID, defined as string constant</span><br /><br />    <span style="color:#007F00; font-style:italic;">// insert event-handling code here</span><br /><br />    <span style="color:#0000FF;"><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Break%20keyword" title="Break keyword (page does not exist)">break</a></span>;<br />}</div>
<p>IMPORTANT: The flag value on a SET event is set only AFTER this script finishes running!
</p>
